{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1513927148,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyODQwOTA1Mjk=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2054","origin":"github"},"title":"Consts should likely not define dir paths including '.git'","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\nIn `consts.py` we define stuff like this:\n\n```\nDATALAD_GIT_DIR = join('.git', 'datalad')\nANNEX_TEMP_DIR = join('.git', 'annex', 'tmp')\n```\n\nI think this is inappropriate, because `.git` can easily be a file. That is why we have `get_git_dir(path)` that will report the actual location of `.git/`, possibly by reading it from a .git file. Such constants should probably just identify the name inside the `.git/` directory.","files":null}]}